<div class="programme twelvecol">
	<div class="twelvecol">
		<h2 class="title"><a href="https://silverscreenfolkestone.savoysystems.co.uk/SilverScreenFolkestone.dll/TSelectItems.waSelectItemsPrompt.TcsWebMenuItem_1047128.TcsWebTab_1047129.TcsProgramme_4566077">George Michael: The Faith Tour</a> <img src="https://folkestonecinema.com/wp-content/themes/silverscreen-child/images/BBFC_12A_RGB.png" alt="Certificate 12A" height="25" style="height:25px;"></h2>
		<p><p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">George Michael was one of the most influential stars of his generation; his voice and songwriting defined an era. Assembled from rediscovered, previously unseen and unheard 35mm footage of his 1988 performance at the Palais Omnisports de Paris-Bercy, this new concert film captures George at the height of his creative power during the record-breaking Faith Tour. Expertly restored and remastered, the film transforms a defining cultural moment into a spectacular cinema experience. An original short film by Mary McCartney opens the feature, using newly discovered audio and imagery from 1986&#8211;1988 &#8211; the Faith era &#8211; creating a rare and intimate &#8216;time capsule&#8217;, offering a vivid insight into George&#8217;s mindset at this pivotal moment in his life.</span></p>
</p>
